>>
Rule 1 (Probability value for dropout must be between 0 and 1 inclusive)
{v_1 : float} |= (v_1 ≥ 0) ∧ (v_1 ≤ 1)
>>
Rule 2 (Check if the shape of the input tensor has at least one dimension when training is enabled)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if v_2 then ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (The data type of the input tensor must be a floating-point type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 8)
>>
Rule 6 (The data type of the input tensor should not be complex if training is enabled)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if v_2 then (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10)
>>
Rule 7 (Check if the scale factor is greater than zero)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 8 (If training is enabled and p > 0 then scale factor should be 1/(1-p))
{v_1 : float, v_2 : bool, v_3 : float} |= if v_2 ∧ (v_1 > 0) then v_3 = (1 / (1 - v_1))
>>
Rule 14 (If inplace is true, the input tensor should not be read-only. Always False for functional dropout)
{v_1 : bool} |= v_1 = false
>>
Rule 18 (If the dropout probability is 0, the result should be same as the input. So it's not necessary to calculate dropout)
{v_1 : float} |= if v_1 = 0 then true
>>
Rule 19 (If the dropout probability is 1, all the elements are zero.)
{v_1 : float} |= if v_1 = 1 then true
>>
Rule 23 (The dropout probability should not be greater than 0.5 if training is true and the input tensor has a large number of elements - approximated)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float, v_3 : bool} |= if v_3 ∧ (ndim(v_1) > 2) then v_2 ≤ 0.5
>>
Rule 30 (The input tensor's dimension should be greater than or equal to 1.)
{v_1: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
